# Account Warm-up

Modular monolith: `backend/src/acwa` serves the API and the worker, `frontend` is a separate React app. Do not add Celery, Redis, Kafka, or extra services.

Keep business rules on the backend. The browser never calls DeepSeek or Threads and never receives API keys or tokens.

Do not invent external endpoints, scopes, or fields. Documented contracts live in `docs/configuration.md`.

Update the matching doc and `backend/openapi.json` plus generated frontend types when behavior or the HTTP contract changes. Do not edit `frontend/src/api/schema.d.ts` by hand.

Do not publish to Threads during startup, migrations, or tests. Live publishing happens only when `ACWA_INTEGRATION_MODE=live` and the user starts a publish.

This install is a single local owner. `ACWA_AUTH_TOKEN` is required; without that password the API and UI stay closed.
